<article class="env-definition" id="06FY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06FY">Definition <span data-tag="06FY">101.18.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{X}$ be an algebraic stack. We say a point $x \in |\mathcal{X}|$ is a <em>finite type point</em><a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001724869" id="a0001724869-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> if the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/06FX" data-tag="06FX">101.18.1</a> are satisfied. We denote $\mathcal{X}_{\text{ft-pts}}$ the set of finite type points of $\mathcal{X}$. </p>
</article>